  planner_response {
    modified_response: "I have updated the Members section to completely replace the hardcoded `MOCK_MEMBERS` with real Firebase Firestore and Storage operations as requested.\n\nHere is a summary of the functionality that has been implemented in `app/page.tsx`:\n\n1. **Load Members (Real-Time)**: `MembersView` now queries the `members` collection using Firebase endpoints on component mount. We handle loading spinners state (`isLoading`) natively while the snapshot is parsed.\n2. **Add & Edit Member**: \n   - `AddMemberModal` now supports both Creating and Editing depending on whether pre-filled `memberData` is provided.\n   - It mathematically calculates the `expiryDate` by checking the selected plan (Monthly 30, Quarterly 90, Half-Yearly 180, Annual 365) from `startDate` logic and auto-categorizes the `status`. \n   - Image upload logic hooks into `firebase/storage`, generating a specific path via `members/{memberId}/photo` and pulling back a signed `getDownloadURL()`.\n   - Creating a user also writes to `payments` using `addDoc(...)`.\n3. **Delete Action (Batching)**: Tapping Delete launches a confirmation prompt. Acceptance runs a `writeBatch()` to drop the `member`, along with `attendance` and `measurements` docs tied to the corresponding `id`. \n4. **Real-time Status Check**: Prior to loading members, the frontend fires a batched background job. If it spots records hitting `< today` or within `< next 7 days`, it dynamically flips the flag to `Expired` or `Expiring Soon` using `updateDoc`. \n5. **Search & Filtration**: A segmented `where(\'status\', \'==\', filter)` handles dropdown views via Firestore queries natively. Searches by phone + name run blazing-fast directly over the state payload.\n6. **Member Profile Modal**: Tapping a user expands their `MemberProfile`. Leveraging `getDoc`, it asynchronously queries `payments` and `attendance` via Firebase (utilizing their explicit `orderBy` instructions)."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
